<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-21T11:48:30+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:48:30 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[China’s vegetation restoration linked to groundwater drought from 2003 to 2015]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135082802.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Vegetation restoration on the Loess Plateau started in 1999, which caused a significant decline in groundwater storage levels. From 2003 to 2015, researchers observed rapid vegetation growth alongside worsening groundwater drought conditions. The decline in groundwater was statistically significant and affected a larger area with more severe drought. Satellite data provided insights into the relationship between vegetation growth and groundwater drought across the region.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/china-began-restoring-vegetation-across-the-loess-plateau-in-1999-scientists-later-found-groundwater-drought-intensified-as-vegetation-expanded-between-2003-and-2015/articleshow/135082802.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/china-began-restoring-vegetation-across-the-loess-plateau-in-1999-scientists-later-found-groundwater-drought-intensified-as-vegetation-expanded-between-2003-and-2015/articleshow/135082802.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T11:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135082928,imgsize-258995.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kandinsky painting stolen by Nazis sells for $42M at auction]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135049497.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A painting by Wassily Kandinsky, titled Das bunte Leben, sold at auction for £31.56 million. This artwork was returned to the heirs of its original Jewish owners after decades of dispute. The piece was originally painted in 1907 and displayed at notable exhibitions. Following its theft by the Nazis, it changed hands multiple times before being held by a German bank.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-kandinsky-masterpiece-stolen-by-the-nazis-in-1940-was-returned-to-the-heirs-of-its-jewish-owners-in-2023-the-1907-painting-has-now-sold-at-auction-for-nearly-42-million/articleshow/135049497.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-kandinsky-masterpiece-stolen-by-the-nazis-in-1940-was-returned-to-the-heirs-of-its-jewish-owners-in-2023-the-1907-painting-has-now-sold-at-auction-for-nearly-42-million/articleshow/135049497.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T11:04:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135049512,imgsize-81320.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Who is next Republican nominee for US Prez? Vance expects endorsement; Trump says 'no']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135079753.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US President Donald Trump has declined to endorse Vice President JD Vance for the 2028 presidential election. While Vance expects Trump's support if he runs, Trump did not commit to backing him. Trump stated there are many capable individuals who could succeed him in the future. Vance acknowledged he hadn't discussed his candidacy directly with Trump. Both their remarks highlight the uncertain nature of the upcoming Republican nomination contest.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/who-is-the-next-republican-nominee-for-us-president-jd-vance-expects-2028-endorsement-trump-says-no/articleshow/135079753.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/who-is-the-next-republican-nominee-for-us-president-jd-vance-expects-2028-endorsement-trump-says-no/articleshow/135079753.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T09:05:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135080963,imgsize-83824.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[When superheroes hit the streets: Batman, Spider-Man &amp; Cap.America at France protests - watch]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135080380.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Recent protests in France saw participants dressed as superheroes like Captain America, Batman, and Spider-Man. While demonstrations began with student grievances, they broadened to include various groups united against rising living costs. In cities like Marseille and Paris, clashes with police erupted, where costumed figures captured attention amid the unrest. Additionally, historical figures such as Napoleon were also spotted among demonstrators.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/avengers-assemble-from-captain-america-to-spider-man-superheroes-run-wild-as-france-protests-turn-violent/articleshow/135080380.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/avengers-assemble-from-captain-america-to-spider-man-superheroes-run-wild-as-france-protests-turn-violent/articleshow/135080380.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T08:57:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135081456,imgsize-11800607.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Queensland farmer reports cloudy well amid 96-million-litre water extraction plan]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135082496.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-queensland-farmer-says-his-familys-140-year-old-well-turned-cloudy-after-neighbouring-water-tests-the-council-has-rejected-a-bottling-plant-linked-to-a-96-million-litre-annual-groundwater-licence/articleshow/135082496.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-queensland-farmer-says-his-familys-140-year-old-well-turned-cloudy-after-neighbouring-water-tests-the-council-has-rejected-a-bottling-plant-linked-to-a-96-million-litre-annual-groundwater-licence/articleshow/135082496.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T10:27:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135082569,imgsize-1620425.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dev Rai founded a nonprofit at 15; it has helped 400 artisans, sold 900 products and mobilised 300 volunteers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135049146.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At just 15 years old, Dev Rai launched Serving Society Global Foundation, aiming to uplift India's traditional artisans. This growing nonprofit has generated over $15,000 and engaged more than 300 volunteers. By creating essential connections between artisans and American consumers through community initiatives, Rai envisions a future where these artisans can thrive through digital platforms, enhancing cultural heritage while empowering youth in entrepreneurship and leadership roles.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-dev-rai-the-indian-american-virginia-student-who-founded-a-nonprofit-at-15-to-help-artisans-in-india-two-years-later-it-has-supported-over-400-craftspeople-sold-900-products-and-mobilised-300-volunteers/articleshow/135049146.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-dev-rai-the-indian-american-virginia-student-who-founded-a-nonprofit-at-15-to-help-artisans-in-india-two-years-later-it-has-supported-over-400-craftspeople-sold-900-products-and-mobilised-300-volunteers/articleshow/135049146.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T09:58:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135049244,imgsize-1456358.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Stephen Hawking: “We are just an advanced breed of monkeys on..."]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135081596.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA