imes.com/science/discovery/north-carolina-state-university-researchers-turn-laser-beams-into-a-lightsaber-like-antenna-that-sends-radio-signals-without-metal-and-boosts-reception-by-2-5-times/articleshow/135066810.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/north-carolina-state-university-researchers-turn-laser-beams-into-a-lightsaber-like-antenna-that-sends-radio-signals-without-metal-and-boosts-reception-by-2-5-times/articleshow/135066810.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T22:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135066886,imgsize-528230.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pete Davidson sells Staten Island condo at a $400,000 loss after listing in 2026]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135067532.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pete Davidson sold his Staten Island condominium for $800,000, taking a substantial loss on the property. He had previously purchased the condo for $1.2 million and completed renovations after acquiring it. Davidson also struggles to sell his North Salem estate, which has undergone multiple price reductions since being listed. The estate features amenities such as a gourmet kitchen and a gaming room, appealing to potential buyers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/pete-davidson-sold-his-staten-island-condo-at-a-400000-loss-the-comedian-had-owned-the-property-before-putting-it-on-the-market-in-2026/articleshow/135067532.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/pete-davidson-sold-his-staten-island-condo-at-a-400000-loss-the-comedian-had-owned-the-property-before-putting-it-on-the-market-in-2026/articleshow/135067532.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T09:20:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:cr