ow/135071085.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T09:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135071148,imgsize-1317038.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Falling water levels at Utah’s Great Salt Lake exposed mysterious circular mounds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135071376.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Newly released satellite images reveal an array of circular mounds at Great Salt Lake, predominantly formed by freshwater springs, which significantly contribute 12% to the lake’s water levels. Researchers, during expeditions across the receding lakebed, confirmed this essential finding. The unique circular reeds at the mound centers highlight the presence of these freshwater sources, which could also aid in controlling dust emissions from exposed areas.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/falling-water-levels-at-utahs-great-salt-lake-exposed-mysterious-circular-mounds-freshwater-springs-beneath-them-may-supply-up-to-12-of-the-lakes-water-budget/articleshow/135071376.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/falling-water-levels-at-utahs-great-salt-lake-exposed-mysterious-circular-mounds-freshwater-springs-beneath-them-may-supply-up-to-12-of-the-lakes-water-budget/articleshow/135071376.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T04:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135071470,imgsize-107798.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A newly built Nando’s drive-through in Australia sold for $5.845 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135071586.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A newly built Nando's drive-through site in Cranbourne North has been acquired for $5.845 million by a New South Wales investor. The development includes a dual-lane drive-through facility and is secured by a long-term lease with Nando's Australia, ensuring an anticipated annual net income of $319,035, alongside fixed rent hikes of 3%. The transaction indicates a rising trend in commercial property investments in Victoria, particularly from out-of-state buyers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-newly-built-nandos-drive-through-in-australia-sold-for-5-845-million-its-15-year-lease-generates-319035-a-year-with-rent-rising-3-annually/articleshow/135071586.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-newly-built-nandos-drive-through-in-australia-sold-for-5-845-million-its-15-year-lease-generates-319035-a-year-with-rent-rising-3-annually/articleshow/135071586.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T08:15:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135071660,imgsize-132715.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin Uber driver father in NYC seeks help on GoFundMe for daughter's funeral after mother kills five-year-old: 'I lost my whole world']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135076657.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-uber-driver-father-in-nyc-seeks-help-on-gofundme-for-daughters-funeral-after-mother-kills-five-year-old-i-lost-my-whole-world/articleshow/135076657.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-uber-driver-father-in-nyc-seeks-help-on-gofundme-for-daughters-funeral-after-mother-kills-five-year-old-i-lost-my-whole-world/articleshow/135076657.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T01:51:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135076668,imgsize-142144.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A DB Cooper ransom bill found in 1980 sold for $134,200 at auction in 2026]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135076547.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A fragment of a D.B. Cooper hijacking banknote fetched an impressive $134,200 at a Dallas auction. This particular note was part of the $200,000 ransom paid to the infamous hijacker back in 1971. Interestingly, in 1980, a young boy came across a piece of this ransom money at Tena Bar, which was later confirmed as authentic by the FBI.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1971-a-hijacker-vanished-with-200000-in-1980-an-8-year-old-found-part-of-the-ransom-on-a-washington-riverbank-and-a-damaged-20-note-from-the-discovery-sold-for-134200-at-auction-in-2026/articleshow/135076547.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1971-a-hijacker-vanished-with-200000-in-1980-an-8-year-old-found-part-of-the-ransom-on-a-washington-riverbank-and-a-damaged-20-note-from-the-discovery-sold-for-134200-at-auction-in-2026/articleshow/135076547.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T01:47:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135076664,imgsize-804262.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['As a second-generation Indian-American': 21-year-old Vasant Bhatt says he voted for Democrat Talarico in Texas election after being disgusted by MAGA racism]]></title><description>&lt;img 